E0201: An operator is used on values of the wrong types

Why it happens:
  Arithmetic needs two numbers of the same type (two ints or two floats); + also joins two
  strings. int and float never mix, and nothing is converted for you.

Example:
    print(1 + "a")
    print(2 * 1.5)

How to fix it:
  Convert one side on purpose: to_string(x), float(x), int(x).
